# Test dependencies. tests/requirements.txt pins them, and every package
# they pull in, with the hashes of their files: pip then installs exactly
# those files, also on the self-hosted CI runner, which installs them on
# every run (docs/adr/0005). Resolved for the build host's Python, 3.12 on
# Linux x86_64. After a change here, regenerate it with uv
# (https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), from the repository's root:
#
#   uv pip compile tests/requirements.in --python-version 3.12 \
#       --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --generate-hashes \
#       -o tests/requirements.txt
